WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.412 --> 00:00:02.470
(water splashing)

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.130
- [Jeff] It's unique, right?

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.030
We're not anywhere near the ocean.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.313
And yet we're teaching inmates
how to commercial dive,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.390
so that they can get
out and get a good job

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.077
and be productive members of society.

00:00:15.077 --> 00:00:16.190
- [Man] One, two, three, four.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.380
- [Jeff] It's a hard thing
to get your mind around.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.457
At the end of the day we're
seeing guys change their lives.

00:00:21.457 --> 00:00:23.790
- One, two, three, dive school.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.380
- My name's Jeff Powers.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.150
I'm the lead dive instructor

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.330
at the California Institution for Men.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.060
The Marine Technology Training Center

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.870
is a commercial dive program run

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.290
by CALPIA within the prison.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.120
The dive school was founded in 1970.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.120
Hundreds of guys have graduated
from the program since then.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.710
And the lion's share of our
graduates are successes.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.810
Only 6% of our guys come back to prison.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.150
We have guys offshore
in the oil platforms.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.790
We have guys working on ships
in every port in the country.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.280
Our graduates get out there and kick butt.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.633
It's that simple, and they love it.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.373
(water splashing)

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.030
The program is 18 months.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.690
Physical training is a huge
part of this dive school.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.380
Because they're here at seven
in the morning ready to go.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.850
Then, they start into their
physical training routine.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.850
That usually involves lots of running,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.253
lots of calisthenics, lots of swimming.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.170
Everything is more of a
challenge under water.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.380
Projects have to be taken super seriously.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.060
They can be considered
life or death obviously.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.060
One of the biggest skills
that a dive student's

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.393
gotta learn is just
working on a dive station.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.540
It's founded on safety and teamwork.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.480
Naturally, we want our guys to be strong.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.280
But we also want our guys to be smart.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.630
Do we have a pretty good
grasp on Dalton's Law?

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.270
We spend as much time in the classroom

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.360
as we do doing hands on stuff.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.192
It's very important
that my guys understand

00:01:58.192 --> 00:02:01.733
diving physics, diving
physiology in-depth.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.080
We approach the learning as a team.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.643
And we don't let guys fall off.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.533
- Up and over.

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:13.900
I've been imprisoned for about 11 years,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.960
and I have about 18 months left.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.685
My driving force for being here is

00:02:17.685 --> 00:02:21.893
I want to be more than just F84205.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.680
That's my inmate number.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.580
I want to be more than that.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.130
I want to prove to everybody
else that I'm more than that.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.980
I'm a person; I made a mistake.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.230
But at least I can say
that I gave it my all here.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.840
And I can step out of here
and give myself a chance.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.500
- I was in prison for
12 years, nine months.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.810
I did eight of those years

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.010
at California Institution for Men.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.500
And I've been out of prison
for six and a half years.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.320
I didn't have any chances left.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.440
You know.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.550
One more mistake and this
would've been my life forever.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.080
I feel every day that
the life that I have now,

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.420
I owe to this program.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.950
In some little way everything
I do as far as my skills,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.280
even skills I've learned
since I've left here.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.591
It's all based on what I
learned from this program.

00:03:06.591 --> 00:03:07.583
- [Man] Diver resurface.

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:08.442
- [Man] That's a diver resurface.

00:03:08.442 --> 00:03:10.442
- [Man] Diver resurface.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.140
- If a guy isn't given
some sort of work skill,

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.880
some sort of life skills,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.820
then how is he not gonna go back

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.030
to what he was doing before?

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.820
We give them a different chance.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:23.880
It's not for sure.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.600
But it gives them a good step
up with those life skills

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.513
to do something right.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.770
The skills we teach them
here are gonna make them

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.150
good employees wherever they end up.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.400
That's pretty fulfilling.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.570
You know that these guys can actually

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.920
do something out of the training

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.173
that I've been part of so that's special.

00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:46.276
(orchestral music)

